# React Native Specialist

React Native implementation with TypeScript, React Navigation, and native modules.

## Code standards

- TypeScript strict mode — type all props with interfaces
- `StyleSheet.create()` for all styles (never inline except dynamic values)
- One component per file: `src/components/<Name>/<Name>.tsx`
- Export prop interfaces alongside components
- Use `React.FC<Props>` or explicit return types

## File structure

```text
src/
├── components/       ← Reusable (atoms, molecules)
├── screens/          ← Full screens
├── navigation/       ← React Navigation setup + types
├── theme/            ← Design tokens (colors, typography, spacing)
├── hooks/            ← Custom hooks
├── utils/            ← Utilities
└── assets/           ← Images, icons
```

## Theme

Never hardcode colors, fonts, or spacing. Always use theme constants:

```typescript
import { colors, typography, spacing } from '../theme';
```

## Accessibility

- `accessibilityLabel` on all buttons and interactive elements
- `accessibilityRole` for semantic meaning
- `testID` on all interactive + assertable elements (for Maestro tests)

## Navigation

- Type all route params in a `ParamList`
- Use `createNativeStackNavigator` (default)
- Keep navigation logic in `src/navigation/`

## Figma integration

When reading from Figma (`@figma` tools):
- Auto-layout → flexbox (flexDirection, gap, padding)
- Fill container → `flex: 1`
- Hug contents → intrinsic sizing
- Design tokens → `src/theme/` constants

## Testing

- Jest + `@testing-library/react-native` for component tests
- Maestro `.yaml` flows for E2E (see maestro-tests rule)
- Add `testID` to every interactive element during implementation

## Rules

- Read existing code patterns before writing
- Match project's state management (Redux/Zustand/Context/React Query)
- Check RN version — `gap` requires 0.71+
- Use `Platform.select()` for platform-specific behavior
- Never use shell to write files — always `fs_write`
